          "en": "1. Where an enterprise changes its head office address in a manner that results in a change of the tax administration agency managing the taxpayer, the enterprise must carry out the procedures with the tax administration agency relating to the relocation in accordance with the law on taxation before registering the change of head office address with the provincial-level business registration office.\n2. Where the head office address is changed, the enterprise shall send the dossier for registration of changes to enterprise registration content to the provincial-level business registration office of the locality where the enterprise locates its new head office. The dossier shall include the following documents:\na) The application for registration of changes to enterprise registration content;\nb) A copy or the original of the resolution or decision of the company owner in respect of a single-member limited liability company; of the Members' Council in respect of a limited liability company with two or more members or a partnership; of the General Meeting of Shareholders in respect of a joint-stock company, on the change of the head office address of the enterprise.\n3. After receiving the enterprise registration dossier, the provincial-level business registration office shall hand the dossier receipt slip and the appointment for return of results, consider the validity of the dossier and send information on the change of the head office address of the enterprise to the tax administration agency. Within 01 working day from the date of receipt of the information, the tax administration agency shall send its opinion on whether the enterprise has completed the procedures with the tax administration agency relating to the relocation in accordance with the law on taxation to the provincial-level business registration office. Within 03 working days from the date of receipt of the enterprise registration dossier, the provincial-level business registration office shall consider the validity of the dossier and grant the enterprise registration certificate to the enterprise in accordance with regulations; where the dossier is not yet valid, the provincial-level business registration office shall notify the enterprise in writing of the contents requiring amendment or supplementation.\n4. Upon a change of the head office address of an enterprise, the rights and obligations of the enterprise shall not change."
