        "text": {
          "en": "1. Where the legal representative of a company is changed, the company shall send the dossier for registration of changes to enterprise registration content to the provincial-level business registration office of the locality where the company has its head office. The dossier shall include the following documents:\na) The application for registration of change of the legal representative;\nb) A copy or the original of the resolution or decision on the change of the legal representative of the company owner in respect of a single-member limited liability company; of the Members' Council in respect of a limited liability company with two or more members; of the General Meeting of Shareholders in respect of a joint-stock company where the change of the legal representative alters the content of the charter of the company, or of the Board of Directors where the change of the legal representative does not alter the content of the charter of the company other than the content of personal information and signature of the legal representative prescribed in Article 24 of the Law on Enterprises.\n2. The person signing the application for registration of change of the legal representative shall be one of the following individuals:\na) The Chairman of the Members' Council or the Chairman of the Company in respect of a limited liability company. Where the Chairman of the Members' Council or the Chairman of the Company is the legal representative, the person signing the application shall be the newly appointed or elected Chairman of the Members' Council or Chairman of the Company;\nb) The Chairman of the Board of Directors in respect of a joint-stock company. Where the Chairman of the Board of Directors is the legal representative, the person signing the application shall be the newly elected Chairman of the Board of Directors;\nc) Where the Chairman of the Members' Council or the Chairman of the Board of Directors is absent or unable to perform his or her rights and obligations, the person signing the application for registration of change of the legal representative shall be the person authorised by the Chairman of the Members' Council or the Chairman of the Board of Directors. Where there is no authorised member, or the Chairman of the Members' Council or the Chairman of the Board of Directors dies, is missing, is detained, is serving a prison sentence, is subject to an administrative handling measure at a compulsory drug rehabilitation establishment or compulsory education establishment, has absconded from the place of residence, has restricted or lost civil act capacity, has difficulties in perceiving and controlling his or her acts, or is prohibited by the Court from holding office, practising a profession or doing certain work, the person signing the application for registration of change of the legal representative shall be the person temporarily elected as Chairman of the Members' Council or Chairman of the Board of Directors in accordance with clause 4 Article 56, clause 3 Article 80 and clause 4 Article 156 of the Law on Enterprises;\nd) Where the owner of a single-member limited liability company being an individual is detained, is serving a prison sentence, is subject to an administrative handling measure at a compulsory drug rehabilitation establishment or compulsory education establishment, has restricted or lost civil act capacity, or has difficulties in perceiving and controlling his or her acts, the authorised person or the representative prescribed in clause 2 and clause 5 Article 78 of the Law on Enterprises shall be the person signing the application for registration of change of the legal representative.\n3. Where the legal representative is changed in accordance with clause 6 Article 12 of the Law on Enterprises, the dossier for registration of change of the legal representative shall include the documents prescribed in clause 1 of this Article, in which the copy or the original of the resolution or decision of the Members' Council shall be replaced by a copy of the document confirming that the legal representative of the company has died, is missing, is being prosecuted for criminal liability, is detained, is serving a prison sentence, is subject to an administrative handling measure at a compulsory drug rehabilitation establishment or compulsory education establishment, has absconded from the place of residence, has restricted or lost civil act capacity, has difficulties in perceiving and controlling his or her acts, or is prohibited by the Court from holding office, practising a profession or doing certain work. In this case, the person with authority to sign the application for registration of change of the legal representative shall be the remaining member of the company.\n4. Where an enterprise registers a change of the legal representative concurrently with the registration of a change or a notification of a change of enterprise registration content, the updating or supplementation of enterprise registration information, or the correction of enterprise registration information, except in the case of registration of a change of the owner of a single-member limited liability company, the person with authority to sign the application for registration of change of the legal representative, the applications and notices of change of other contents in the enterprise registration dossier, and the document authorising the carrying out of enterprise registration procedures shall be the individual prescribed in clauses 2 and 3 of this Article.\nAfter receiving the enterprise registration dossier, the provincial-level business registration office shall hand the dossier receipt slip and the appointment for return of results to the dossier submitter. Within 03 working days from the date of receipt of the enterprise registration dossier, the provincial-level business registration office shall consider the validity of the dossier and grant the enterprise registration certificate to the enterprise in accordance with regulations; where the dossier is not yet valid, the provincial-level business registration office shall notify the enterprise in writing of the contents requiring amendment or supplementation."
        },
