          "en": "1. Within 03 working days from the date of receipt of the decision of the Court to open bankruptcy procedures, the provincial-level business registration office shall post the decision on the national business registration portal and change the legal status of the enterprise to the status of undergoing bankruptcy procedures and the legal status of its branches, representative offices and business locations to the status of undergoing procedures for termination of operation in the national database on enterprise registration.\n2. Within 03 working days from the date of receipt of the list of creditors, the provincial-level business registration office shall post the list of creditors on the national business registration portal.\n3. Within 03 working days from the date of receipt of the decision of the Court declaring the enterprise bankrupt, the provincial-level business registration office shall post the decision on the national business registration portal and change the legal status of the enterprise to the bankrupt status and the legal status of its branches, representative offices and business locations to the status of terminated operation in the national database on enterprise registration.\n4. Information on the enterprise being in the process of bankruptcy procedures or having become bankrupt, and on its branches, representative offices and business locations being in the process of termination of operation or having terminated operation, shall be transmitted to the tax registration application system for updating."
