          "en": "1. Information connected and shared with the national database on enterprise registration in order to enhance the effectiveness of State management of enterprises must ensure currency and accuracy in accordance with the law.\n2. The connection and sharing of information shall not affect the rights and responsibilities of the relevant organisations and individuals; it must be used for the right purpose and comply with the regulations on confidentiality, security and safety of network information.\n3. The managing agency of the national database and of the specialised databases shall be responsible for carrying out information management and data governance activities and for ensuring the readiness for connection and sharing of information with the national database on enterprise registration in accordance with this Decree, the law on management, connection and sharing of information and the relevant law.\n4. The data-owning agency and the managing agency of the national database and of the specialised databases shall be responsible for developing regulations on coordination in the management and connection and sharing of information on enterprises between the national database on enterprise registration and the national databases and specialised databases. The regulations shall include the following main contents:\na) The list of shared information fields;\nb) The data format, and the definition and description of the relevant attributes of the information fields;\nc) The method and frequency of connection and sharing of information;\nd) The conditions ensuring connection and sharing, including: the characteristics and technical standards of the information technology infrastructure, human resources and finance;\ne) Regulations on the use and confidentiality of the information provided."
